## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F3 | open | BLOCKING | js/unit-tests/test_instructionRefs.js | 🚨 blocking the rework that crap split walk broke v1shimindex — r13 s moved target guard is now dead code always green never fires the crap split hunk this rework flipped the branch order inside walk test instructionrefs js 243 250 the descent branch now runs first for every entry but file exists is an existence check for any path — boolean true in the dmtools host exists true in the node coverage harness node testrunner js 328 predicate function return true so every existing md file enters walk rel file list on a file returns null → zero entries → the else if md … shim read branch at line 248 is unreachable for every real file the index is always evidence — the harness s exact host shapes against the real tree file exists on the shim → exists true file list on it → null shim index size 0 file exists shim md file exists true file list that file null consequence r13 — runner pack refs … never pin a moved target while its v1 shim window is open — can never fire test instructionrefs js 544 589 shims is so var shim shims p if shim … never triggers and the check silently degrades to the dangling pin lookup only the suite still passes — i re ran it under the node harness 20 passed 0 failed — which is exactly why ci cannot see this the guard demonstrably worked at 980ac31a it failed on the pre 980ac31a tree with the exact violation per the discussion the rework disconnected the sensor while keeping the light green this guard is the regression protection for the live agentpackexception crash class this pr itself hit runner pins vs pack contents — merging with it dead re exposes the pr s documented follow up the planned flip of dmtools runners fa review json to the v2 path to the exact failure r13 exists to catch fix two parts 1 restore the read before descend order inside the split structure — md files are files never descent targets javascript if md test rel shimbannerpaths readtext rel foreach function live index live rel else if istrueishexists file exists path fspath rel walk rel 2 pin the composite so this can t regress silently one end to end test asserting v1shimindex contains the 7 shim paths e g index instructions pr review review verdict rules md instructions pr review review verdict rules md the new characterization suite pins the four helpers but nothing pins the assembled index — that is the gap that let a green suite ship a dead guard |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

# PR new hunks — what changed since the last review concluded

Last reviewed head: 274de967284f27e446d4053e1ebe689e99651599
Current head: e4740df4c1cf4eefad4a79f833499b49768f57fa

These hunks are the re-review scope, together with their interaction
neighborhood (direct callers/callees of changed symbols). Every line
NOT shown here is frozen: a finding on an unchanged line must show that
these hunks make the problem worse (the interaction test) — otherwise
it is advisory digest only, never a review thread.

--- diff ---

diff --git a/js/unit-tests/test_instructionRefs.js b/js/unit-tests/test_instructionRefs.js
index 5cf67e07e..79d3c6d79 100644
--- a/js/unit-tests/test_instructionRefs.js
+++ b/js/unit-tests/test_instructionRefs.js
@@ -227,12 +227,22 @@ function shimBannerPaths(txt) {
 }

 // file_list shape normalization + the dotfile skip: repo-relative entry
-// names in host order, hidden entries dropped.
-function listRelEntries(dir) {
-    var out = file_list(fsPath(dir));
+// names in host order, hidden entries dropped. NOT a directory → null:
+// file_list THROWS on a file in the dmtools host (FileSystemException
+// "Not a directory" — pr-1465 canonical suite crashed R13 descending into
+// instructions/review/base.json) but returns null in the node coverage
+// harness — both spellings must read as "not a directory".
+function dirEntriesOf(dir) {
+    var out;
+    try {
+        out = file_list(fsPath(dir));
+    } catch (eList) {
+        return null;
+    }
+    if (out === null || out === undefined) return null;
     if (typeof out === 'string') out = JSON.parse(out);
-    var entries = (out && out.entries) || [];
-    return entries.map(function (e) {
+    if (!out || !out.entries) return null;
+    return out.entries.map(function (e) {
         var s = String(e).replace(/\\/g, '/');
         return s.slice(s.lastIndexOf('/') + 1);
     }).filter(function (n) { return n[0] !== '.'; });
@@ -241,12 +251,20 @@ function listRelEntries(dir) {
 function v1ShimIndex() {
     var index = {};
     function walk(dir) {
-        listRelEntries(dir).forEach(function (name) {
+        var names = dirEntriesOf(dir);
+        if (!names) return;
+        names.forEach(function (name) {
             var rel = dir + '/' + name;
-            if (isTrueishExists(file_exists({ path: fsPath(rel) }))) {
-                walk(rel);
-            } else if (/\.md$/.test(rel)) {
+            // Branch order IS the sensor: file_exists is truthy for plain
+            // FILES (both host shapes), so the .md read must come FIRST —
+            // descent-before-read sent every real .md into walk(rel), where
+            // file_list on a file yields no entries and the index silently
+            // degraded to {} with the suite green (R13 dead, pr-1465
+            // review 2026-11-13). .md files are files, never descent targets.
+            if (/\.md$/.test(rel)) {
                 shimBannerPaths(readText(rel)).forEach(function (live) { index[live] = rel; });
+            } else if (isTrueishExists(file_exists({ path: fsPath(rel) }))) {
+                walk(rel);
             }
         });
     }
@@ -588,6 +606,41 @@ suite('instructionRefs — v1-shim index helpers (pr-1465 characterization)', fu
             'instructions/pr_review/base/output_rules.md'
         ]);
     });
+
+    // Host-shape pin for the walk's descent guard: file_list on a FILE
+    // throws in the dmtools host and returns null in the node harness —
+    // dirEntriesOf must map BOTH spellings to null ("not a directory"),
+    // so the walk never crashes on a file inside instructions/ (pr-1465
+    // canonical dmtools suite: R13 crashed on instructions/review/base.json).
+    test('dirEntriesOf: a file path reads as "not a directory" (null); a real directory lists entries', function () {
+        assert.equal(dirEntriesOf('js/unit-tests/test_instructionRefs.js'), null,
+            'a file path must normalize to null, not entries and not a throw');
+        var dirEntries = dirEntriesOf('instructions');
+        assert.ok(Array.isArray(dirEntries) && dirEntries.length > 0,
+            'a real directory still lists its (dotfile-skipped) entries');
+    });
+
+    // Composite pin (end-to-end, real tree): the helper pins above cannot
+    // see a broken ASSEMBLY — the pr-1465 CRAP-split reordered walk's
+    // branches (descent before the .md read), and since file_exists is
+    // truthy for plain files, every real .md entered walk() and the index
+    // silently degraded to {} with the suite still green (R13's guard dead
+    // without a single red). This test IS that sensor: the index must map
+    // every live target a shim banner names back to the shim path.
+    test('v1ShimIndex: end-to-end over the real tree — all 7 shims map their live targets (livePath -> shimPath)', function () {
+        var index = v1ShimIndex();
+        var expected = {
+            'instructions/pr_review/generalist/few_shots.md': 'instructions/pr_review/few_shots.md',
+            'instructions/pr_review/base/formatting_rules.md': 'instructions/pr_test_automation_review/formatting_rules.md',
+            'instructions/pr_review/generalist/lens.md': 'instructions/pr_review/general_guidelines.md',
+            'instructions/pr_review/base/input_context.md': 'instructions/pr_review/output_rules.md',
+            'instructions/pr_review/base/registry_protocol.md': 'instructions/pr_review/general_guidelines.md',
+            'instructions/pr_review/base/output_rules.md': 'instructions/pr_test_automation_review/output_rules.md',
+            'instructions/pr_review/base/review_verdict_rules.md': 'instructions/pr_review/review_verdict_rules.md'
+        };
+        assert.deepEqual(index, expected,
+            'v1ShimIndex drifted from the real shim set (a dead index returns {})');
+    });
 });

